rtl8xxxu: do not RTS/CTS every HT frame on 8188EU

ampdu_enable was set true for all HT QoS data, and fill_txdesc_v3
enables RTS/CTS whenever ampdu_enable is set. That puts RTS on
every TCP ACK before a BA session exists, so 8188EU rate control
stays at MCS 0 and downloads sit around 50 KB/s.

Only mark the frame as A-MPDU after IEEE80211_AMPDU_TX_OPERATIONAL.
Still start the BA session the same way.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Ben Klopfenstein <benklop@gmail.com>

---
 rtl8xxxu_core.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/rtl8xxxu_core.c b/rtl8xxxu_core.c
--- a/rtl8xxxu_core.c
+++ b/rtl8xxxu_core.c
@@ -5659,7 +5659,11 @@ static void rtl8xxxu_tx(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 			val32 = ampdu << TXDESC_AMPDU_DENSITY_SHIFT;
 			tx_desc->txdw2 |= cpu_to_le32(val32);
 
-			ampdu_enable = true;
+			/* Only treat the frame as A-MPDU once the BA session is up.
+			 * ampdu_enable=true on every HT QoS frame forced RTS/CTS
+			 * (fill_txdesc_v3) and pinned 8188EU RA at MCS 0 (~50 KB/s).
+			 */
+			ampdu_enable = test_bit(tid, priv->tid_tx_operational);
 
 			if (!test_bit(tid, priv->tx_aggr_started) &&
 			    !(skb->protocol == cpu_to_be16(ETH_P_PAE)))
